<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nepherites II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 380 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nepherites II was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> of the Twenty-ninth Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakor">Hakor</a>. He reigned only a few months in 380 BCE before being deposed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nectanebo-i">Nectanebo I</a>, a general from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sebennytos">Sebennytos</a>, who founded the Thirtieth Dynasty, the last native dynasty of ancient Egypt.</p></div>
